{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01JypKWLKdQquFR8u16xUmNz","type":"tool_result","content":"lib.rs\n--- confirm no mutation residue in src/lib.rs ---\nclean: no mutation residue\n--- key lines intact ---\n42:///     uint32_t next, cache = 0, s = bs->pos & 7;\n57:    // `bs->pos & 7`: bitwise and on the two's complement representation, so the\n59:    let s: u32 = ((*bs).pos & 7) as u32;\n66:    if (*bs).pos > (*bs).limit {\n69:    let mut next: u32 = (*p as u32) & (255u32 >> s);\n76:        cache |= next.wrapping_shl(shl as u32);\n135:                    let half: c_int = 1i32.wrapping_shl((ba - 1) as u32).wrapping_sub(1);\n145:                    let m: u32 = (2i32.wrapping_shl((ba - 17) as u32) as u32).wrapping_add(1);\n163:    group_size.wrapping_mul(4)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b04777ce-727a-4a51-96d2-12393b2b1cc7","uuid":"ed6955c0-5bfe-44dc-9f27-5e3075ea1c06","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:06:54.680Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"lib.rs\n--- confirm no mutation residue in src/lib.rs ---\nclean: no mutation residue\n--- key lines intact ---\n42:///     uint32_t next, cache = 0, s = bs->pos & 7;\n57:    // `bs->pos & 7`: bitwise and on the two's complement representation, so the\n59:    let s: u32 = ((*bs).pos & 7) as u32;\n66:    if (*bs).pos > (*bs).limit {\n69:    let mut next: u32 = (*p as u32) & (255u32 >> s);\n76:        cache |= next.wrapping_shl(shl as u32);\n135:                    let half: c_int = 1i32.wrapping_shl((ba - 1) as u32).wrapping_sub(1);\n145:                    let m: u32 = (2i32.wrapping_shl((ba - 17) as u32) as u32).wrapping_add(1);\n163:    group_size.wrapping_mul(4)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_2pz7civzfcwqiyom4a4gk4axczz4osedwlf337eklwvenrbvjnxq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases pass.\n\n## Outcome: **no divergences found — the Rust translation is byte-identical to the C**\n\nThe library is small (2 C functions: exported `dequantize_granule`, `static get_bits`), so I could verify it exhaustively rather than by sampling.\n\n### Phase A — surface mapping (`translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`)\n- **SYMBOLS.md** — C `.so` exports exactly one symbol, `dequantize_granule`; the Rust `.so` exports it in both debug and release. Diff is empty, 0 undefined non-libc symbols. `get_bits` is `static` in C and correctly stays private in Rust. No C module was skipped, no stubs exist.\n- **ERRORS.md** — 25 rows. The library has *no* error macros, enums, asserts, or null checks; its only real rejection is the `get_bits` underrun guard `if ((bs->pos += n) > bs->limit) return 0;` (a sentinel, with the side effect that `pos` advances anyway). I also enumerated the UB conditions that crash *both* implementations identically and documented why they're excluded rather than silently skipped.\n- **CONFIGS.md** — 41 rows over the axes the C actually branches on: `total_bands` (0/1/32/33-64/65-255, the latter two reading out of bounds into `scfcod` and past the struct), every `bitalloc` opcode 0..255, `group_size` (negative/0/1..576), all 8 bit-phase alignments, `limit` regimes, and bitstream shapes.\n\n### Phases B & C — differential tests (`tests/`, 69 tests)\nBoth `.so`s are loaded with `libloading`; **no Rust function is ever called directly**. Each case compares return value, mutated `bs->pos`/`bs->limit`, the full 8192-slot `grbuf` bit-for-bit, and asserts neither library mutates its inputs.\n\n### Phase D — gate\nSymbol diff empty in both profiles; all 41 + 25 rows checked off; `scripts/check_feature_combos.sh` derives the combination set from `Cargo.toml` (no `[features]` → `{default, --no-default-features}` × `{debug, release}` = 4 configs) and all pass.\n\n### The part that makes \"no divergence\" meaningful\nA passing differential suite proves nothing unless it would catch a real bug, so I added `scripts/mutation_check.py`, which injects mistranslations into `src/lib.rs`, rebuilds, and re-runs everything. **All 15 were caught** — including the subtle ones this code is full of: `>` vs `>=` on the underrun guard, not advancing `pos` on failure, unmasked shift counts (`2 << (ba-17)` masked to 5 bits, so `ba` aliases with period 32; `ba==47` overflows `int` to make `mod == 0x80000001`; `ba==48` gives `mod == 1`), signed vs unsigned `mod/2`, clamped `bitalloc` indexing, and the alternating `+576 / -558` `choff` walk. The one mutation I predicted was *provably* behaviour-preserving (hoisting `choff`'s init into the `j` loop, equivalent because `2*total_bands` is always even) survived, as expected.\n\nAs a robustness check the whole suite also passes against a `-O2` rebuild of the C.\n\n### Changes I made\nOnly `translation/`: added `libloading` to `[dev-dependencies]`, the three Phase A docs, `tests/{common,layout,phase_b,phase_c}`, and `scripts/`. **`src/lib.rs` needed no fixes** and is byte-identical to how I found it (verified after mutation testing restored it); `c_src/` was not modified apart from the `build/` directory the instructions asked me to create."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":949,"cache_read_input_tokens":159247,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":949,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b04777ce-727a-4a51-96d2-12393b2b1cc7","uuid":"e5c1129f-ed2a-478b-9c67-448fb71e5f8f","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:07:14.473Z"}
